# .env is the first entry for a reason: it carries live provider keys, the Fernet
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY that decrypts stored OAuth and Instagram Page tokens, and the
# database URL. An image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier one. Secrets
# reach a container at RUN time -- a k8s Secret, envFrom -- never at build time.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

.git
.github
.venv
venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.DS_Store

# Not runtime: the suite, the writing, the dev log spool, scratch uploads.
tests
docs
logs
files
*.md
!README.md

# Never copy a build recipe or a run plan into the thing it builds.
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
deploy
k8s

# Terraform, and the provider binaries it caches. Nothing here is ever COPYed,
# but everything here is uploaded to the daemon as build context -- and
# infra/*/.terraform alone is several hundred megabytes on a machine that has
# run `terraform init`.
infra
.codegraph
